.TH GA4 1 "September 2026" "ga4-omarchy 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ga4 \- Google Analytics 4 terminal dashboard for Omarchy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ga4
.br
.B ga4 auth login --client-secret
.I PATH
.br
.B ga4 properties
[\fB--json\fR]
.br
.B ga4 export --property
.I ID
.B --start
.I DATE
.B --end
.I DATE
.B --format
.I csv|json
[\fB--output\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.br
.B ga4 doctor
[\fB--json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ga4
is a keyboard-driven GA4 dashboard. Historical reports are cached locally for
fifteen minutes; OAuth tokens are stored only in the system keyring.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
Create a Google Desktop OAuth client with the Analytics Data and Admin APIs
enabled, then run:
.PP
.B ga4 auth login --client-secret client_secret.json
.PP
Only the analytics.readonly scope is requested.
.SH TUI KEYS
.TP
.B 1, 2
Switch between Overview and Realtime.
.TP
.B Left, Right
Move the selected historical date range.
.TP
.B [, ]
Change the date-range preset.
.TP
.B Tab, j, k, Enter, Esc
Move focus and selection, drill in, or go back.
.TP
.B /, c, p, d, r, e
Filter, compare, select property, enter dates, refresh, or export.
.TP
.B ?, q
Show help or quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ga4-omarchy/config.toml
Preferences without credentials.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ga4-omarchy/oauth-client.json
User-provided Desktop OAuth client definition, mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ga4-omarchy/reports/
Aggregated historical report cache.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 invalid input; 3 authentication required; 4 API configuration or
permission failure; 5 quota limited; 6 network or server failure.
